# 13. NFC FUNCTIONALITY

The NFC card must contain a URL pointing to the customer's public profile.

Example:

https://yourdomain.com/p/jeet-kulkarni

When someone taps a compatible smartphone against the NFC card:

1. Smartphone reads the NFC tag.
2. Smartphone opens the stored public URL.
3. Browser displays the customer's digital business profile.
4. Visitor can save the contact.
5. Visitor can open WhatsApp.
6. Visitor can visit social profiles.
7. Visitor can share the profile.

Important:

The physical NFC tag must be encoded with the same public profile URL represented by the QR code.

The web application cannot write to a physical NFC card remotely.

The printer or card encoding provider must write the URL to the NFC tag during production using compatible NFC encoding equipment.

Include a printer instruction sheet explaining NFC encoding and testing.

Do not claim that every smartphone supports NFC. Provide QR scanning as the universal fallback.

Include a configurable NFC compatibility/help page.

