# 16. FIRESTORE SECURITY RULES

Security is a mandatory requirement.

Implement and provide complete Firestore Security Rules.

Requirements:

- Users can read and update their own permitted account information.
- Users cannot change their own role.
- Users cannot change their own account status.
- Users cannot create admin or SuperAdmin accounts.
- Users cannot access another user's private data.
- Public profile visitors can access only published public information.
- Public visitors cannot read private profile fields.
- Printers can access only assigned orders.
- Printers cannot access unrelated orders.
- Admin access must follow assigned permissions.
- SuperAdmin can manage all application resources.
- Payments cannot be modified by the frontend.
- QR generation and payment verification must be server-side.
- Audit logs must be protected against client-side modification.

Implement equivalent Firebase Storage Rules.

Test the rules using the Firebase Emulator Suite.

